{"availability":"available","full":"codeswithroh/tastemaker","name":"tastemaker","description":"A Claude Code skill that grounds AI-generated UI in real reference images and a persistent per-developer taste profile, instead of generic AI-slop defaults.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":442,"forks":44,"created":"2026-07-09T22:38:40Z","updated":"2026-09-29T10:55:24Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://tastemaker-skill.online","topics":["claude-skills","codex-skill","kimi-skill","ui-skill"],"demo":"https://tastemaker-skill.online/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:30:44.561Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:30:44.561Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:30:44.561Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T14:33:25.566Z","stars":431,"forks":39},{"at":"2026-10-04T16:12:47.014Z","stars":432,"forks":39},{"at":"2026-10-06T17:12:46.067Z","stars":437,"forks":40},{"at":"2026-10-08T22:30:44.561Z","stars":442,"forks":44}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A skill that gives AI real design taste, so the UI it builds does not look AI-generated.","Ask any model to build a UI and you tend to get the same thing: an indigo to purple gradient, a soft shadow card, a generic hero. This is not a prompting problem. It happens because the model has to invent taste from a text description, with nothing real to ground it and no memory of what you actually like.","Tastemaker fixes this with four ideas, not a bigger catalog of canned options to pick from:"],"features":["Generate within a check that actually runs. There is no fixed list of color combinations shipped with this skill, and the palette is not five approved colors the model may combine however it likes either. A new one is…","Ground in real pixels, not words. Give it a screenshot or a reference and it reads the real colors and contrast from the actual image, using a script. It does not write a vague summary of the vibe and rebuild from that.…","Remember, do not re-derive. Once a project locks a style, every later screen reuses it. Nothing drifts. Across projects, a small profile file learns what you keep and what you reject, so your next project starts warm.","Scope to the real work. It reads your spec first and figures out which screens actually need design, instead of dumping a design system that has nothing to do with what you are shipping."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/codeswithroh/tastemaker/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1ce6813bb71d063fa56d0ff4830030214e2c3f04c70a5431ebcbb3483687d8d5","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T07:02:03.327Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:16:55.933Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A skill that gives AI real design taste, so the UI it builds does not look AI-generated.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/codeswithroh/tastemaker/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"There is no hosted backend, no account, and no API key.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/codeswithroh/tastemaker/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"1ce6813bb71d063fa56d0ff4830030214e2c3f04c70a5431ebcbb3483687d8d5","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/codeswithroh/tastemaker/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T14:16:55.934Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-29T10:55:24Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:16:55.938Z","overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T10:48:51.916Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/codeswithroh/tastemaker/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T14:27:23.266Z","hash":"1ce6813bb71d063fa56d0ff4830030214e2c3f04c70a5431ebcbb3483687d8d5","originalBytes":20670,"storedBytes":20670,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["tastemaker","real","palette","same","nbsp","one","project","what","which","contrast","every","may","mood","read","skill","check","color","design","does","references","text","two","carry","install","skills","first","just","motion","build","code"